== Parallel timelines ==
Independent timelines that share a row and wrap when there is no room. Narrow the window to see them wrap.

{{TimelineRail/parallel
|{{TimelineRail |title=Players
|{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex8 |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=March 2016 |title=Lee Sedol wins game 4}}
}}
{{TimelineRail |title=Programs
|{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex9 |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo wins the match}}
}}
}}

== Parallel and grouped timelines ==
The same two timelines, grouped: the dots line up horizontally (at 640 px and wider; below that they fall back to the independent layout).

{{TimelineRail/parallel |grouped=yes
|{{TimelineRail |title=Players
|{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex10 |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{TimelineRail/gap}}
{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex11 |date=March 2016 |title=Lee Sedol wins game 4}}
}}
{{TimelineRail |title=Programs
|{{TimelineRail/gap}}
{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex12 |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{TimelineRail/item |id=ex13 |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo wins the match}}
}}
}}

